# Session Handoff — Cold-Start Install Refactor

## Context

User removed `/aide:init` and shifted cold-start to `npx aidemd-mcp init`. The CLI now installs every canonical AIDE artifact (8 categories) without needing a Claude Code session. To make this work end-to-end, this session also built the **runtime side** of the handoff:

- A new boot-time MCP tool (`aide_info`) that reports brain vault state to the orchestrator.
- An inline-recovery flow in the `/aide` orchestrator that completes vault-path setup AFTER cold install. The CLI deliberately writes an empty-vault-path obsidian entry; the orchestrator picks up the handoff.

The two halves are inseparable — without the runtime side, the CLI's empty obsidian entry would never get completed.

