## Outstanding Bug — FIXED & VERIFIED (2026-04-24, continuation)

**The orchestrator's 1-hint case was incorrectly skipping `AskUserQuestion` and falling back to inline prompt.**

### What's happening

User in `D:/Code/Me/aide-fresh` (after `/aide:upgrade` pulled the orchestrator fix):

```
One step left before the pipeline can run: wiring up the obsidian MCP entry's vault path so AIDE
has a brain to persist research and retros into.

The obsidian MCP entry is already in .mcp.json — it just needs a vault path.
I detected a candidate at D:\Code\Me\my-brain (sibling hint).
Reply with that path to use it, or paste a different absolute path.
```

^ That's the inline 1-hint branch firing. User wanted the clickable picker UX (`AskUserQuestion`).

### Why the current logic was over-engineered

`AskUserQuestion`'s schema enforces `options.minItems: 2`. With 1 hint, `[hintOption]` would fail validation. The current fix sidesteps this by going inline for 0 and 1 hints. But the original test retry (BEFORE this session's fix) showed that adding an explicit `"Other"` option DOES work — the schema's "There should be no 'Other' option, that will be provided automatically" recommendation is a UX hint, not a hard rule.

### Correct fix

Always use `AskUserQuestion` when at least 1 hint exists. Always include explicit Other as the last option:

| Hint count | Options array | Total |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | inline prompt only (can't satisfy `minItems: 2`) | n/a |
| 1 | `[Use {hint.path}, Other]` | 2 ✓ |
| 2 | `[hint1, hint2, Other]` | 3 ✓ |
| 3 | `[hint1, hint2, hint3, Other]` | 4 ✓ (at `maxItems: 4`) |

If 3 hints + explicit Other hits `maxItems: 4` and `resolveBrainHints` ever returns 4 hints (currently impossible — only env/sibling/conventional sources exist), drop the lowest-priority hint to make room for Other.

If duplicate-Other in the UI turns out to be a real problem (test retry showed it works, but UI dedup wasn't verified), use `"Different location"` as the explicit-option label instead — functionally identical, semantically distinct from auto-Other.

### Where it was fixed

`.claude/commands/aide.md` lines 48–67 — replaced 3-branch (0/1/2+) logic with 2-branch (0 hints inline / ≥1 hints picker). The picker now includes an explicit `"Different location"` final option to satisfy `AskUserQuestion`'s `minItems: 2` schema constraint while keeping the auto-provided "Other" UX intact (`"Different location"` label distinguishes it from the auto-Other to avoid duplicate-Other ambiguity in the UI).

Step 2 resolver collapsed accordingly: picker case (≥1 hint) extracts hint path from the label OR custom text from `"Different location"` / auto-Other; inline case (0 hints) uses the user's reply verbatim.

